    "level": "workflow",
    "title": "Adapt provider failures without losing response-body diagnostics",
    "summary": "Use when multiple provider SDKs encode HTTP failures differently and catch paths expose only opaque messages. Do not replace already-useful messages unconditionally, duplicate body or metadata content, remove existing provider prefixes/hints, or emit unbounded response bodies. Establish a normalized error contract, format it conditionally, integrate it at request failure boundaries, reconcile provider-specific decorations, and validate both helpers and representative end-to-end catch paths.",
